/-!
# Base change of Eisenstein extensions and preservation of lower ramification

Let `R → R'` be a homomorphism of discrete valuation rings under which `maximalIdeal R` generates
`maximalIdeal R'`, such as the residue-field enlargement `R → CompletedResidueExtension R L` of
*ÉGA III*, Chap. 0, 10.3.1. Because every uniformizer of `R` remains a uniformizer of `R'`, the
normalized additive valuation is preserved on `R`, and every polynomial `f : R[X]` that is
Eisenstein at `maximalIdeal R` remains Eisenstein at `maximalIdeal R'` over `R'`.

When `B` is generated over `R` by a root `x` of a monic Eisenstein polynomial `f`, the powers
`1, x, …, x ^ (deg f - 1)` have valuations in distinct congruence classes modulo `deg f`, so
`addVal B (aeval x p)` is determined solely by the valuations in `R` of the coefficients of
`p %ₘ f`. Consequently:

* `AdjoinRoot f ≃ₐ[R] B`, and for any domain `B'` generated over `R'` by a root `x'` of
  `f.map (algebraMap R R')`, the induced `R`-algebra homomorphism `B →ₐ[R] B'` sending `x ↦ x'`
  preserves normalized additive valuations (`addVal B' (j b) = addVal B b`).
* Any group homomorphism `ρ : H →* H'` intertwining actions on `B` and `B'` on the Eisenstein
  generator preserves normalized displacement valuations `addVal (σ • x - x)`, Serre's lower index
  `lowerIndex`, and the integer- and real-indexed lower ramification filtrations `ramificationGroup`
  and `ramificationGroupReal`.
* At the fraction-field level `K = Frac R`, `K' = Frac R'`, `f.map (algebraMap R K')` is
  irreducible over `K'`, and in any field extension `E' / K'` generated by a root `α` of `f` (in
  particular `E' = AdjoinRoot (f.map (algebraMap R K'))`), the integral closure of `R'` in `E'` is
  `R'[α]`, a discrete valuation ring of degree `deg f` over `K'`.
* When `E / K` is a finite Galois extension whose integral closure `integralClosure R E` is
  generated over `R` by a root `x` of `f`, `E' / K'` is also Galois and there is a canonical group
  isomorphism `galMulEquiv : (E ≃ₐ[K] E) ≃* (E' ≃ₐ[K'] E')` preserving `addVal (σ • x - x)`,
  `lowerIndex`, `ramificationGroup`, `ramificationGroupReal`, and their cardinalities.

## Main definitions and results

* `TauCeti.IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal_algebraMap_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`: an unramified
  homomorphism of discrete valuation rings preserves `IsDiscreteValuationRing.addVal`.
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.map_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`: Eisenstein polynomials remain Eisenstein
  along an unramified homomorphism of discrete valuation rings.
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.addVal_aeval_of_natDegree_lt`: power-basis valuation formula for a
  root generating an Eisenstein extension of discrete valuation rings.
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.adjoinRootAlgEquiv` and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.baseChangeAlgHom`: presentation `AdjoinRoot f ≃ₐ[R] B` and
  valuation-preserving base-change map `B →ₐ[R] B'` (`addVal_baseChangeAlgHom`).
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.lowerIndex_eq`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.comap_ramificationGroup`, and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.comap_ramificationGroupReal`: preservation of lower indices and lower
  ramification groups under equivariant Eisenstein base change.
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.irreducible_map_fractionRing_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq` and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.integralClosure_eq_adjoin_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`: irreducibility over
  `K'` and identification `integralClosure R' E' = Algebra.adjoin R' {α}`.
* `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.isGalois_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.galMulEquiv`,
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.map_ramificationGroup_galMulEquiv`, and
  `Polynomial.IsEisensteinAt.card_ramificationGroupReal_eq`: preservation of the Galois group and
  of the lower ramification filtration.

## References

* A. Grothendieck and J. Dieudonné, *Éléments de géométrie algébrique III*, Chapitre 0,
  Proposition 10.3.1.
* [J.-P. Serre, *Corps Locaux*][serre1968], Chapter I, §6 and Chapter IV, §1, Proposition 1.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

